# Code Style

Write self-explanatory code through good names and small, single-purpose
functions. Prefer early-return guard clauses over deep nesting.

## Formatting

- No semicolons, single quotes, 2-space indentation (Prettier enforces this).
- `verbatimModuleSyntax` is on: import types with `import type { X }`.
- Imports are sorted by `import/order` (builtin → external → internal →
  sibling/parent → index, alphabetized, no blank lines between groups). Run
  `npm run lint:fix` rather than hand-sorting.

## Naming & structure

- Descriptive, verb-first functions (`resolveSelectedModel`, `registerThemeHandlers`,
  `normalizeShortcuts`).
- `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for module-level constants (`MODEL_EXTENSION`,
  `DEFAULT_SHORTCUTS`, `DEFAULT_LOCALE`).
- Extract private helpers at module scope; keep the exported surface obvious.
- Pass a named `interface` options object when a function takes several params
  (e.g. `RegisterModelHandlersOptions`).

## Types

- `interface` for object shapes; `type` for unions and aliases.
- Model variants as discriminated unions (see `LlamaStreamEvent`); use
  `as const` arrays/objects for enum-like sets (`LOCALES`, `SHORTCUT_ACTIONS`,
  `IpcChannels`) and derive types with `(typeof X)[number]`.
- Let return types infer when obvious; annotate only when it adds clarity or safety.
- `strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, and `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` are on —
  handle `undefined` from index access and don't pass `undefined` to optional props.

## Error handling

- Swallow-and-fallback for non-critical reads (return `[]`/`null`), as in
  `listModels`.
- For actionable failures, throw an `Error` with your own user-facing message and
  log the raw error separately with `logger` — never surface a caught error's
  `.message` directly.

## Comments

Default to zero comments. Add one only when it explains something the code cannot:
a non-obvious "why", trade-off, caveat, or library/platform quirk.

- Never narrate the code, restate a name, or log your edit (`// added retry`).
- No commented-out code, section banners, or redundant JSDoc.
- When suppressing a lint rule, justify it inline
  (`// eslint-disable-next-line ... -- reason`).
